.Dd March 3, 2026
.Dt LD 1
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm ld
.Nd Substrate ELF linker for i386 and x86-64
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl m32 | Fl m64 | Fl m Ar emulation
.Op Fl r | Fl shared | Fl pie | Fl static
.Op Fl o Ar output
.Op Fl e Ar symbol
.Op Fl L Ar dir
.Op Fl l Ar name
.Op Fl Bstatic | Fl Bdynamic
.Op Fl -start-group ... Fl -end-group
.Op Fl -whole-archive | Fl -no-whole-archive
.Op Fl -as-needed | Fl -no-as-needed
.Op Fl T Ar script
.Op Fl -gc-sections
.Op Fl -print-gc-sections
.Op Fl -icf Ns = Ns Ar safe|all|none
.Op Fl -hash-style Ns = Ns Ar sysv|gnu|both
.Op Fl -allow-undefined | Fl -no-undefined
.Op Fl -unresolved-symbols Ns = Ns Ar ignore-all|report-all
.Op Fl -undefined Ar symbol
.Op Fl -defsym Ar name=value
.Op Fl -trace
.Op Fl -trace-symbol Ns = Ns Ar symbol
.Op Fl -warn-common
.Op Fl -fatal-warnings
.Op Fl -z Ar text|notext|execstack|noexecstack|relro|norelro
.Op Fl -plugin Ar path
.Op Fl -plugin-opt Ar option
.Op Fl -Map Ar file
.Op Fl -reproduce Ar dir
.Op Fl -compat Ns = Ns Ar gnu|lld
.Op Fl -version
.Op Fl -help
.Ar input ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the native Substrate linker implementation for ELF inputs.
It links
.Dv ET_REL
objects and archives into relocatable, executable, and shared outputs.
It does not forward to external linker backends.
.Pp
When no target mode is forced,
.Nm
auto-selects i386 or x86-64 mode from the first compatible input.
.Pp
For
.Fl l
resolution,
.Nm
searches
.Fl L
paths first, then host defaults
.Pa /usr/lib
and
.Pa /usr/local/lib .
Both regular ELF libraries and GNU ld script wrappers
.Pq Dv INPUT / Dv GROUP
are supported.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--unresolved-symbols=report-all"
.It Fl m32 , Fl m64 , Fl m Ar emulation
Select output architecture mode.
.It Fl r
Produce relocatable
.Dv ET_REL
output.
.It Fl shared , Fl pie
Produce
.Dv ET_DYN
output.
.It Fl static
Prefer static archive resolution.
.It Fl L Ar dir , Fl l Ar name
Add a library search directory and request a library.
.It Fl Bstatic , Fl Bdynamic
Toggle static/dynamic library lookup mode for subsequent
.Fl l
operands.
.It Fl -start-group ... Fl -end-group
Repeatedly scan grouped libraries until no new unresolved symbols are satisfied.
.It Fl -whole-archive , Fl -no-whole-archive
Force extraction of all archive members for subsequent
.Fl l
or archive inputs.
.It Fl -as-needed , Fl -no-as-needed
Control whether DSOs without currently unresolved symbol matches are ignored.
.It Fl T Ar script
Use a linker script.
.It Fl -gc-sections
Enable section garbage collection.
.It Fl -print-gc-sections
Print removed sections while doing
.Fl -gc-sections .
.It Fl -icf Ns = Ns Ar mode
Enable identical code/data folding in
.Ar safe
or
.Ar all
mode.
.It Fl -hash-style Ns = Ns Ar style
Select dynamic symbol hash style.
.It Fl -defsym Ar name=value
Define or override an absolute symbol.
.It Fl -undefined Ar symbol
Force a symbol into the unresolved root set.
.It Fl -allow-undefined , Fl -no-undefined
Set unresolved symbol policy.
.It Fl -unresolved-symbols Ns = Ns Ar policy
GNU-style unresolved symbol policy alias.
.It Fl -trace , Fl -trace-symbol Ns = Ns Ar symbol
Trace input loading and symbol usage.
.It Fl -z Ar option
Set text-relocation, stack-execute, and RELRO policy.
.It Fl -plugin Ar path
Set plugin executable used for LTO materialization.
.It Fl -plugin-opt Ar option
Pass plugin-specific options.
.It Fl -Map Ar file
Write a link map including inputs, sections, program headers, and symbol provenance.
.It Fl -reproduce Ar dir
Write a reproducible link bundle containing object snapshots, manifest, and replay script.
.It Fl -compat Ns = Ns Ar gnu|lld
Set unsupported-option policy for compatibility behavior.
.El
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
Diagnostics are emitted in parser-friendly one-line forms such as
.Dq ld: error: ...
and
.Dq ld: warning: ... .
For select classes,
.Nm
adds structured notes with category/source/hint metadata.
.Sh COMPATIBILITY NOTES
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Nm
implements GNU-compatible options for the supported feature set but is not a full GNU ld script superset.
.It
GNU plugin shared-object API is not loaded directly;
.Fl -plugin
expects an executable materializer interface.
.It
Behavior for unsupported options differs by
.Fl -compat
mode.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr as 1 ,
.Xr cc 1 ,
.Xr readelf 1 ,
.Xr elfobj 3
